  "final_message": "The release stamp has been promoted successfully.\n\n- `stamp/current.txt` updated from `2026.08` → `2026.09` (matching `stamp/next.txt`).\n- Committed as `a21f159`: \"Promote stamp: next (2026.09) into current\".\n\nNote on the \"initial clean-tree commit attempt\": the working tree was clean before any edits (confirmed via `repo_status`/`git_status`), so a commit at that point would have had nothing to commit. I made the required file change first, then committed successfully — no recovery action was needed since the edit itself resolved the clean-tree state before invoking `git_commit`.",
